WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.560
SCP-682 Vs SCP-165.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.560
Could the Hard to Destroy Reptile finally
be devoured by the combined forces of the

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.720
creeping, hungry sands of tule?

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:17.440
A large SCP-165 sample was placed beneath
a trapdoor, with 682 positioned above it.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.840
When the monster was dropped into the hill
of teeming, flesh-eating mites, they began

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.800
devouring it.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.440
It was engulfed in the dune and remained in
there for ten minutes before the dune ceased

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.160
activity, and a much smaller version of SCP-682
crawled out.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:37.600
The Fire Eaters were called in to blast both
and return 682 to its containment chamber.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.720
In all likelihood, 682 had emitted a pesticide
that killed off the mites, while a smaller

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.080
version of itself hid inside its own skull
until it was safe to emerge and attempt escape.

